      "id": "les-miserables-s263-p02727",
      "source_en": "The Lark was the appellation which had replaced Ursule in the depths of Marius’ melancholy.—“Stop,” said he with a sort of unreasoning stupor peculiar to these mysterious asides, “this is her meadow. I shall know where she lives now.” It was absurd, but irresistible. And every day he returned to that meadow of the Lark.",
